#
# Conformance case: teleology/concurrent-composition.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition program combinator (parallel/concurrent operator)
# is declared over two sub-programs: monitorSensors (left operand) and
# executeMotion (right operand) advance together with their elementary steps
# interleaved over a shared path. This pins the structural vocabulary and the
# key distinction: ConcurrentComposition is the COMPOSITION OPERATOR, DISTINCT
# from the three separately-declared concurrency correctness concerns —
# logic:SerializabilityCriterion (a history property), logic:IsolationLevel
# (a declared guarantee strength), and logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (an
# implementation mechanism). Those concerns govern HOW concurrent histories are
# controlled; ConcurrentComposition is the structural operator that NAMES that
# two programs run concurrently.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live
# in input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/concurrent-composition/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
